            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0802" n="652" xml:id="pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6775/134.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of Honduras
                        to President Roosevelt.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa, Honduras</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 26,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>November next having been agreed on as the time for the meeting in your city of
                    the Central American Peace Conference, I respectfully ask that Your Excellency,
                    continuing your friendly offices, will consent to appointing a representative
                    who would take part in the said conference. Confident of your gracious assent, I
                    tender to you in advance my heartfelt thanks.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Miguel E. Dávila.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
